## About the framework

The NIST Cybersecurity Framework (CSF) is a voluntary framework for understanding, managing and communicating cybersecurity risks. Version 2.0 was released in 2024 and broadened the framework to organisations of all sizes and sectors.

## The functions

The framework is built around six functions:

1. **[Govern](/ramverk/nist-csf/govern)** – leadership and governance of cybersecurity work
2. **[Identify](/ramverk/nist-csf/identify)** – understand assets and risks
3. **[Protect](/ramverk/nist-csf/protect)** – safeguards and capabilities
4. **[Detect](/ramverk/nist-csf/detect)** – detection of incidents
5. **[Respond](/ramverk/nist-csf/respond)** – handling when an incident occurs
6. **[Recover](/ramverk/nist-csf/recover)** – recovery after an incident

## Relation to EU regulation

The CSF is not legislation, but many organisations use it as a structure for meeting NIS2's risk management requirements.
